[38;2;124;124;124mIf "smooth" means $C^\infty$ sample paths, then certainly the paths are $C^1$, [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mhence bounded variation on compact intervals, hence quadratic variation is zero.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mIf "smooth" means $C^1$ sample paths, same conclusion.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mEven if "smooth" just means continuous, that's not enough — Brownian motion is [0m
